Instantiation Doctrine

Thesis

Communication is not the transmission of words.

It is the instantiation of a compatible internal model inside another cognitive system.

The medium is negotiable.

The instantiated structure is the objective.

⸻

General Equation

\boxed{
I(M,T,C)
\rightarrow
\hat{S}
}

Where:

* M = medium (story, music, mathematics, code, image, conversation)
* T = transformation protocol
* C = shared context
* \hat{S} = reconstructed internal simulation

The receiver never receives the original thought.

They instantiate their own approximation.

